commit fa2fb8fd3839ea4548e342b2080aa6e35802e5b3

C03: a screen reading is recognized in the mission-completed shape and its quoted lines are observed data (SCREEN1413)

SCREEN1411 measured the grounded reading contract and found three gaps. The final of a two-step mission composes from the mission-completed situation (steps as JSON strings, completedStepsInOrder in the payload), not from a single ocr.read operation: the quoting instruction and the grounding check keyed on a top-level operation never applied, and an unfounded summary passed. When a draft did quote recognized lines, the App and the mind vetoed it as internal code because a code-heavy screen carries identifiers, paths and dotted names. And the five-second composition ceiling cut every attempt that quoted more than one line.

baxy_mind.observed_response_literals: a verified ocr.read step (single or inside steps) supplies its recognized lines and identifier tokens to the vocabulary exemption, as window titles and process names already do.
Baxy.App.ObservedResponseLiterals: the same exemption for the App's lexical checks.
baxy_mind.llm: _recognized_screen_text / _recognized_screen_text_in_situation find the OCR text in both shapes; the quoting instruction and ocr_unsupported_terms use them.
Baxy.App.MindSidecarClient: a verified screen reading of 512 characters or more, single or as a mission step, receives the dense composition timeout (10 s on GPU) instead of the 5-second ceiling.

App recompiled (BUILD1413). Tests not run (owner order).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>


